Drop the pinned server verifying key here as a file named `phantom_server_pk`
(no extension), containing the RAW bytes emitted by the CLI `pubkey` command —
NOT hex text. It becomes `R.raw.phantom_server_pk` and is read by
PhantomServerConfig.load(). See the repo-root README of this sample for the
exact keygen/pubkey commands.

NEVER fetch this key at runtime — baking it in at build time is what makes the
server-pinning trust model (Security Invariant 1) sound. If the resource is
absent, PhantomServerConfig falls back to a non-functional demo hex constant so
the project still compiles.
